From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:50:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: mtk_ccci: Quietly drain CCCI_CH_IMSM_RX channel

The MT6789 Gen95 modem periodically sends 32-byte IMS service status
packets on logical channel 169 (CCCI_IMSM_RX). Without an IMS daemon
active, these hit the unhandled default path and spam kernel warnings
and hex dumps in dmesg.

Define CCCI_CH_IMSM_RX (169) and drain it quietly at debug level.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci.h      | 1 +
 drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci_core.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci.h b/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci.h
index a1b2c3d4e..f5e6d7c8b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci.h
@@ -112,6 +112,7 @@
 #define CCCI_CH_RPC_TX			33
 #define CCCI_CH_STATUS_RX		67
 #define CCCI_CH_STATUS_TX		68
+#define CCCI_CH_IMSM_RX			169
 
 /* Control channel message IDs */
 #define CCCI_MD_INIT_START_BOOT		0x0
diff --git a/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci_core.c b/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci_core.c
index 34c9d42d6..777777777 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci_core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/mtk_ccci_core.c
@@ -885,6 +885,10 @@ static void mtk_ccci_drain_queue(struct mtk_ccci_dev *ccci, u32 q)
 		case CCCI_CH_UART2_RX:
 			mtk_ccci_at_rx(ccci, ccci->rx_buf, ret);
 			break;
+		case CCCI_CH_IMSM_RX:
+			dev_dbg(ccci->dev, "CCIF Q%u IMSM RX len=%d\n",
+				q, ret);
+			break;
 		default:
 			if (__ratelimit(&ccci->unhandled_rs)) {
 				dev_warn(ccci->dev,
-- 
